---
/**
 * /training/agentic-101: the 101's own landing page (website brief, 29 Oct
 * 2026), written to the course-page playbook: what and who, the facts and the
 * one ask on the first screen, "is this for you", the problem, what you'll do,
 * how it runs, a paragraph to forward, then the terms and the ask again.
 * Booking is its only ask: the header, hero, closing band and footer all carry
 * the same 101 ask (asks.ts). Until the booking link exists that ask is an
 * email about a seat; set BOOKING_101_URL in site.ts and every placement
 * switches.
 *
 * Open facts (the exact day, online or in person) come from PILOT_101 in
 * training.ts and read as "I'll confirm" until they're set, never as a guess.
 * The price comes only through the private price gate (priceFor, keyed
 * "agentic-101"); without it every price line says how to get the price.
 *
 * Demos: the brief wants them here before the 1 Dec invitations. None exists
 * yet, so the section isn't rendered; add it above the paragraph to forward
 * when the first demo is ready.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Chapter from "../../components/Chapter.astro";
import Offer from "../../components/Offer.astro";
import { askLink, has101Booking, invoice101Href } from "../../config/asks";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../../config/site";
import { PILOT_101 as pilot, course, priceFor } from "../../config/training";

const intro = course("agentic-101");
const price = priceFor("agentic-101");
const heroAsk = askLink("book-101", "101-hero");
const bandAsk = askLink("book-101", "101-band");
const linkAttrs = (a: typeof heroAsk, placement: string) => ({
  href: a.href,
  target: a.external ? "_blank" : undefined,
  rel: a.external ? "noopener noreferrer" : undefined,
  "data-track": a.event,
  "data-placement": placement,
});

// The facts, written out in "How it runs". An open fact says when it will be
// confirmed.
const when = pilot.day
  ? `${pilot.day}, ${pilot.time}.`
  : `A morning in ${pilot.week}, ${pilot.time}. I'll confirm the day when booking opens.`;
const where = pilot.format
  ? `${pilot.format.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${pilot.format.slice(1)}.`
  : "Online or in person, confirmed with the day.";
const cost = price
  ? `${price} + VAT a seat, the founding rate for this first run.`
  : has101Booking
    ? "A founding rate for this first run. You'll see the price before you pay."
    : "A founding rate for this first run. Email me about a seat and I'll send you the price.";
const forwardPrice = price
  ? `A seat is ${price} + VAT, a founding rate for the first run.`
  : `Seats are at a founding rate for the first run; for the price, email ${CONTACT_EMAIL}.`;
const forwardWhen = pilot.day ? `on ${pilot.day}` : `on a morning in ${pilot.week}`;
// The first screen's fact line: the instrument voice, compact enough that the
// facts and the ask sit above the fold on a laptop.
const heroFacts = [
  `Half a day, ${pilot.time}`,
  pilot.day ?? pilot.week.replace(/^the /, ""),
  pilot.format ?? "online or in person, to be confirmed",
  `${pilot.minSeats} to ${pilot.maxSeats} people`,
  price ? `${price} + VAT a seat, founding rate` : "founding rate",
].join(" · ");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${intro.title}: a half-day course - burningsuit`}
  description="A half-day course for people who build in Power BI but don't write code: hand a change to an AI agent, check what it did, and know which decisions you handed over."
  contactSubject={`The ${intro.title}`}
  ask="book-101"
>
  <Fragment slot="footer-invitation">Tell me what you'd want to hand to an agent first, and I'll tell you whether the 101 will get you there. Replies come from me</Fragment>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="enter appear-300">{intro.title}</h1>
      <p class="lead enter appear-450">A half-day course for people who build in Power BI but don't write code. You'll hand a change to an AI agent (a tool that makes the change itself and shows you what it did), check its work, and know which decisions you handed over.</p>
      <p class="offer-meta enter appear-450">{heroFacts}</p>
      <div class="cta-row routes">
        <a class="cta" {...linkAttrs(heroAsk, "101-hero")}>{heroAsk.label}</a>
      </div>
      {has101Booking ? (
        <p class="hero-sig">You'll pay by card on a secure Stripe page. If your organisation pays by invoice or purchase order, <a href={invoice101Href}>email me</a> and I'll invoice it.</p>
      ) : (
        <p class="hero-sig">The email comes straight to me. I'll reply with the day, the place and the price, and send you the booking link when it's ready.</p>
      )}
      <ul class="routes enter appear-450">
        <li><a class="route" href="#who">Is this for you?</a></li>
        <li><a class="route" href="#what">What you'll do</a></li>
        <li><a class="route" href="#details">How it runs</a></li>
        <li><a class="route" href="#for-whoever-pays">To send to your manager</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="thread" data-reveal-raw aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <Chapter id="who" kicker="Is this for you?">
    <p>You'll need to have built a report in Power BI, even a simple one. You won't need to write code, and you won't need to have used an agent before. You'll do every step yourself, and you'll check every change the agent makes.</p>
    <p>Power BI developers who don't code are welcome. If you already work with coding agents every day, it will cover ground you know.</p>
  </Chapter>

  {/* ALAN: the problem paragraph is drafted from the brief, readers' own
      words in meeting notes, and your 27 Oct "wild west" line; make the
      first person yours. */}
  <Chapter id="problem" kicker="Agents aren't only for developers">
    <p>You build the reports because someone had to. You've probably asked ChatGPT or Copilot for a DAX measure and got one that looked right and didn't work on your model. And everything you read about AI agents building Power BI seems written for people who code. So it's easy to decide agents aren't for you, or to worry that one will break something in the background that you won't be able to find.</p>
    <p>Not long ago, that was fair. Having an agent build something in Power BI was the wild west: full of bugs, and not quite what you'd asked for. I don't think that's true any more, as long as you know which decisions you're handing over and how to check what comes back. That's what this half-day teaches.</p>
  </Chapter>

  {/* ALAN: three items from the brief's three capabilities; confirm them
      against the session plan, and add or swap items (up to six). */}
  <Chapter id="what" kicker="What you'll do">
    <p>You'll work on a Power BI report I've prepared for teaching, and you'll do each step yourself.</p>
    <div class="offer-table">
      <Offer title="Hand over a change">
        <p>You'll ask an agent, in plain English, to make a change to the report, such as adding a measure, and watch it work. Back at your desk, you'll know what these tools can do now, rather than what they could do two years ago.</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer title="Check what it did">
        <p>You'll read what the agent changed and compare the numbers before and after, so you can catch a change that runs without an error and still answers the wrong question. Back at your desk, you'll have a way to check any change, whoever made it.</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer title="Know what you handed over">
        <p>Some decisions are about building, such as how a measure is written. Others are about what your numbers mean, such as what counts as a sale. You'll practise telling them apart and keeping the second kind for yourself. Back at your desk, you'll know what's safe to hand to an agent and what isn't.</p>
      </Offer>
    </div>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="details" kicker="How it runs">
    <div class="offer-table">
      <Offer id="when" title="When and where" meta={pilot.day ? `${pilot.day} · ${pilot.time}` : `${pilot.week.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${pilot.week.slice(1)} · ${pilot.time}`}>
        <p>{when} {where}</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer id="how-long" title="How long, and how many" meta={`${intro.length} · ${pilot.minSeats} to ${pilot.maxSeats} people`}>
        <p>It's a public course, so you book a seat for yourself and can come on your own. There are at least {pilot.minSeats} and at most {pilot.maxSeats} people in the room.</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer id="how-much" title="How much" meta={price ? `${price} + VAT a seat` : "Founding rate"}>
        <p>{cost} If your organisation pays by invoice or purchase order, I'll invoice it instead.</p>
      </Offer>
    </div>
    <p>I teach it myself. It runs on a Power BI report and data I've built for teaching, so you won't bring your own model, and nothing you do touches your organisation's data.</p>
    {/* ALAN: what delegates need installed, which agent, and any licence. */}
    <p>Before the day, I'll send you what to install and a way to check it works.</p>
    <p>Afterwards, I'll ask what worked for you and what didn't. This is the first run, and your answers shape the next one.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="for-whoever-pays" kicker="To send to your manager">
    {/* The paragraph to forward: written to stand on its own when pasted into
        an email to a manager or L&D, in the third person about who'd go. */}
    {/* <wbr> lets the address wrap on a narrow phone without adding
        characters to a copied paragraph. */}
    <p>{intro.title} is a half-day course from burningsuit for people who build reports in Power BI but don't write code. They'll hand a Power BI change to an AI agent, check what it did, and learn which decisions they're handing over, working on prepared examples rather than our own data. It runs {forwardWhen}, {pilot.time}, for {pilot.minSeats} to {pilot.maxSeats} people. {forwardPrice} Details{has101Booking ? " and booking" : ""}: https://<wbr />burningsuit.co.uk/<wbr />training/<wbr />agentic-101/</p>
  </Chapter>

  {/* Terms: the pilot's conditions (29 Oct 2026). Refund and transfer terms
      for someone who can't come are open; add them here before
      BOOKING_101_URL is set. */}
  <Chapter id="terms" kicker="If it moves">
    <p>This is the first run, at a founding rate. It goes ahead with at least {pilot.minSeats} paid seats, and I'll decide on {pilot.goNoGo}. If there are fewer by then, it moves once, to a date in {pilot.movesTo}, and everyone who has booked chooses between that date and a full refund.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-label={bandAsk.label}>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-invite">
        {has101Booking ? (
          <p class="cta-note">Booking takes you to a secure card payment. Paying by invoice or purchase order? <a href={invoice101Href}>Email me</a> instead.</p>
        ) : (
          <p class="cta-note">Nothing is booked or paid until you decide. I'll reply with the day and the price.</p>
        )}
        <a class="cta" {...linkAttrs(bandAsk, "101-band")}>{bandAsk.label}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="thread thread-end" data-reveal-raw aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="talk-spacer"></div>
</BaseLayout>
